+# 4.25 C5 capture adapter (094-35 qualification)
+
+The 4.25 capture adapter now rotates census batches through the shared stencil ledger, using 5.1's inclusive 0.5%–25% coverage band, half-free batch capacity, eight-value event headroom and cycle-aware expiry. Frame requests retain their actor/tag mapping until readback; the next batch restores prior custom-depth flags, stencil values and write masks before reuse. Live event receiver sets receive event-owned values. Default capture follows the player's current view; first-camera selection requires the explicit bench-only override. The 5.1 annotation serializer is ported without changing its schema, with injected membership separated from measured on-screen affected membership. The opt-in C5 bench freezes same-session pose references and unstable maps before scoring; it never saves the map. Real street-map qualification is recorded in the 094-35 journal and receipts.
+
+09435 outcome: the 3,996-frame street session verifies player-view agreement and exact restoration for 1,980 components, including the non-default setup. It does not qualify real-scene labels or anomaly masks: every clean pose exceeds the fixed 5% unstable-pixel limit, so injection stays off. The rotating census measures more than 55 drawn actors at a held pose without exhausting values. Its native legacy bounds-visible counter retains the default 6% bounds floor; the reader derives drawn counts and initial visibility from the independent clean stencil samples instead. Event annotation membership and late-target firing still need a qualified scored session.
